# The ECMA-376 archives the schema-validity suite validates against, pinned by content.
#
# `.github/scripts/fetch-ecma-schemas.sh` downloads each file from
# https://ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/<name> and verifies it against this manifest
# before extracting anything, so a re-upload, a truncated download or a poisoned CI cache is a hard
# failure rather than a silently different schema set. The CI cache is keyed on this file's hash, so
# editing a line here re-fetches automatically.
#
# Part 4 (Transitional) carries the markup schemas: pml.xsd, dml-main.xsd, dml-chart.xsd.
# Part 2 (OPC) carries the packaging schemas: opc-relationships.xsd, opc-contentTypes.xsd.
# Part 1 carries THREE members, extracted from this one download, and no schema this gate validates
# against:
#   * `OfficeOpenXML-XMLSchema-Strict` — the Strict half of the namespace table the generator pairs
#     against Transitional.
#   * `OfficeOpenXML-DrawingMLGeometries/presetShapeDefinitions.xml` — the normative preset-shape
#     corpus. `xtask/tests/published_markup.rs` holds `PresetShapeType`'s wire tokens to it
#     (MJXOFF-250) and `mjx-geometry`'s table is generated from it (MJXOFF-202). Added to CI by
#     MJXOFF-197, because two gates that read it had never once executed there — they skipped, and
#     an absent corpus reads exactly like success.
#   * `OfficeOpenXML-SpreadsheetMLStyles/presetCellStyles.xml` (with `presetTableStyles.xml` beside
#     it) — the only SpreadsheetML markup ECMA publishes, and therefore the only evidence short of a
#     file Office wrote for what a `@theme` position means. `crates/mjx-sml/tests/theme_index.rs`
#     derives the mapping from them rather than restating it (MJXOFF-246).
#
# Its 42 MB is the largest line here and it is deliberate: the outer download is atomic, so the
# part's 35.3 MB PDF cannot be left behind on the server, and only ~1.5 MB is ever extracted. The
# download happens once per cache key, and buying a derived answer with it beats asserting one.
#
# Every hash below is computed from a fresh download off
# https://ecma-international.org/wp-content/uploads/<name> — never from a copy already sitting in a
# developer's `References/`, which is precisely the artefact whose provenance nobody can reconstruct
# later.
bd25da1109f73762356596918bf5ff8b74a1331642dba5f1c1d1dfc6bed34ecd  ECMA-376-4_5th_edition_december_2016.zip
